WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.055
Explore last-in-first-out stacks and first-in-first-out queues.

00:00:05.055 --> 00:00:08.755
The queue removes ticket A first, preserving the arrival order.

00:00:09.755 --> 00:00:12.523
Which item does a queue normally remove first?

00:00:12.523 --> 00:00:16.675
FIFO means first in, first out: the oldest item is removed first.
